      <div class="notice-box">
<strong>Scope:</strong>
No state trial-court docket was read. The Fulton and DeKalb court portals demand a captcha, and Burke County has no online docket, so what happened next in the matters below is unknown where this page says so. The free federal archive holds only dockets that someone has contributed, so absence there is not absence from the federal courts. Each record below stands on its own, with its own date. None is offered as bearing on another.
</div>

<h2>What the Record Says</h2>

<h3>Okpokwu v. Rapid Taxi Company, Inc. et al., U.S. District Court, N.D. Ga., 1:12-cv-02273</h3>

<p>This is a wage suit. It was filed June 29, 2012. The docket gives the cause as "29:216(b) Labor - Minimum wage or overtime compensation". The source is the docket on <a href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/7987715/okpokwu-v-rapid-taxi-company-inc/" target="_blank">CourtListener, the free federal archive</a>, the approval order, and the settlement's released-parties page read by eye from the scan.</p>

<p>On May 29, 2014, docket entry 77 reads "THIRD AMENDED COMPLAINT against Mike Abebe, Addis, Inc., [another individual], Rapid Taxi Company, Inc., Yellow Cab of Georgia, Inc." He is a named defendant from that date. That complaint is not free and was not read, so what it alleges about him is not known here.</p>

<p>On September 12, 2014 a settlement agreement was signed. The source's reading of it is by OCR from a scan. It states a total of "two-hundred fifty thousand dollars ($250,000.00)".</p>

<p>An order signed September 16, 2014 and filed September 17, 2014 "finds that its terms are fair, reasonable, and satisfactory." It approves the agreement and closes the case administratively pending a dismissal. This is the review the law requires for wage settlements. It is not a ruling on any claim.</p>

<p>On March 17, 2015 the case was dismissed with prejudice by stipulation. The source analyst read this on the docket page once; the checker's later fetch of that page was refused.</p>

<p>The settlement's list of released parties, read by eye from the scan, is: "Abebe &amp; Company, LLC; Obtain Enterprises, LLC; Abebe Ventures, LLC; VNC Management, LLC; and Abebe Holdings, LLC." Three of those names are on the entity list the site holds.</p>

<p>This is not a finding of liability. No ruling that the developer or an Abebe entity is liable on any claim was identified in the records opened. The limits on that sentence: no trial docket was read; one order in the wage case, a May 2014 ruling on a sanctions motion made before he was a party, was not read, and nothing is inferred about whom or what it decided; and the court's approval of the settlement is a determination of fairness, not of liability.</p>

<h3>Williams v. Abebe Sandy Ventures LLC, Court of Appeals of Georgia, A22A1200</h3>

<p>The <a href="https://www.gaappeals.gov/wp-content/themes/benjamin/docket/results_one_record.php?docr_case_num=A22A1200" target="_blank">court's docket</a> was found by a search of the court's docket for "abebe" (5 results; two are this case; the other three are individuals with no link to him and are not reproduced). It reads: "Status Remittitur Mailed"; "Remittitur Date March 13, 2023"; "COA Judgment/Ruling REVERSED AND REMANDED (February 24, 2023)"; "Supreme Court Transfer None"; trial court "Case Number 2021CV347317 ... Superior Court Clerk of Fulton County".</p>

<p>What the appeal decided: the docket records that the trial court's judgment was reversed and the case was remanded, with the judgment dated February 24, 2023 and the remittitur mailed March 13, 2023. The source file does not summarize the court's reasoning or say what the underlying claim was.</p>

<p>What it did not decide: the opinion's own footnote, as the source analyst read it, says "We intimate no opinion as to the outcome of any issue in this case on remand." An earlier step, the application to appeal (A22I0091), was granted January 11, 2022 (the source analyst's read).</p>

<p>No later appeal or opinion exists on that docket. What happened in Fulton Superior Court case 2021CV347317 after March 2023 is unknown. The tie, as the first pass read it: the opinion places the company at 249 Milton Avenue SE with Mike Abebe as registered agent.</p>

<h3>Published tax-execution notices that name his entities</h3>

<p>A tax execution notice, as these notices print it, is a legal notice published by a county tax commissioner that lists a parcel, the amount of tax due and a date on which the property may be offered for sale. A legal notice of a sale is not a sale. For each notice below, whether the tax was paid first or any parcel was sold was not seen.</p>

