<p>The tie: the county owner field for each address is an Abebe entity in the matching years; the source notes exceptions in an evidence file that is not published here. On the 948 Donald Lee Hollowell records the portal's own owner field prints the developer's name. On the 249 Milton records it prints another company's name, and on the 1313 Sylvan record an individual's name, not reproduced here. These are reported as displayed.</p>

<h2>What a Party Says</h2>

<p>In the settlement agreement in the wage suit, as the source analyst read it by OCR: "Defendants deny each of the claims asserted against them in the Action and make no admission whatsoever of liability." This is a claim by a party. The complaint's own allegations against the developer were not read.</p>

<p>abebe.com's own page for 249 Milton Ave says, as the source analyst read it: "This site was formerly the headquarters of Yellow Cab, a company proudly owned by Mr. Abebe." This is a statement by a party. It is the source's stated tie between the developer and the Yellow Cab of Georgia, Inc. defendant in the wage suit.</p>

