<h2>What Was Searched and Not Found</h2>

<p>Free federal archive (CourtListener), dockets and opinions, each phrase in quotes: "abebe &amp; company", "abebe and company", "abebe st george", "abebe westside", "abebe inc", the seven other Abebe entity names as one query, "renewal development group", "ensley district developers", "direct invest development", "mekonen abebe", "st. george crossing": 0 results each. "mike abebe": only the two dockets above.</p>

<p>Court of Appeals of Georgia docket, search "abebe": nothing beyond the Williams case. Open-web queries (four) for suits naming the entities: nothing beyond the matters above.</p>

<p>Burke County tax-sale notices for the 2024, 2025 and 2026 seasons (31 weekly posts): no Abebe entity, 249 Milton address or site parcel number. The True Citizen site search for "Abebe", "065027" and "Abebe St George": no legal notice naming an Abebe entity after July 2024.</p>

<p>City permit layers (to January 29 and August 18, 2026): no permit on the five Sylvan and Cox parcels. Fulton County Sheriff's tax and levy sale list for October 6, 2026 (second posting, not final): none of the project parcels and none of the 62 Abebe-entity parcels (the source analyst's read of a scanned list).</p>

<p>No agency enforcement order naming him or an Abebe entity surfaced in the searches run. Not searched: Georgia securities orders, state environmental orders, Alabama courts.</p>

<p>Not searched, which is different from nothing found: any state or county trial docket (Fulton, DeKalb, Burke); the Georgia Supreme Court docket; Alabama courts; "obtain enterprises" on the federal archive (throttled); govinfo full text; Justia. No open deed index was found, and georgiapublicnotice.com and the Fulton Daily Report were not searched.</p>

